{"name":"Shock Jockey","hex":"#bb88aa","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shock","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sudden, heavy impact.","Something so surprising that it is stunning."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Causing intense surprise, horror, etc.; unexpected and shocking."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shock"},{"term":"jockey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who rides racehorses competitively.","That part of a variable resistor or potentiometer that rides over the resistance wire"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To ride (a horse) in a race.","To jostle by riding against."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jockey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jockey","blocks":[{"text":"A jockey is someone who rides horses in horse racing or steeplechase racing, primarily as a profession. The word also applies to camel riders in camel racing. The word \"jockey\" originated from England and was used to describe the individual who rode horses in racing. They must be light, typically around a weight of 100–120 lb. (45–55 kg), and physically fit. They are typically self-employed, and are paid a small fee from the horse trainer, whose colors they wear while competing in a race. They also receive a percentage of the horse's winnings. The job has a very high risk of debilitating or life-threatening injuries, not only from racing accidents but also, because of strict weight restrictions, from eating disorders."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Tony_dobbin.jpg/330px-Tony_dobbin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jockey","wikidata":"Q846750"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Sun_Downs_Kennewick_02.JPG/500px-Sun_Downs_Kennewick_02.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Sun_Downs_Kennewick_02.JPG/1280px-Sun_Downs_Kennewick_02.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Sun_Downs_Kennewick_02.JPG/500px-Sun_Downs_Kennewick_02.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jockey being weighed post-race, holding equipment","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASun_Downs_Kennewick_02.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/%28Albi%29_Le_Jockey_-_1899_-_Henri_de_Toulouse-Lautrec_-_Mus%C3%A9e_Toulouse-Lautrec.jpg/500px-%28Albi%29_Le_Jockey_-_1899_-_Henri_de_Toulouse-Lautrec_-_Mus%C3%A9e_Toulouse-Lautrec.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/%28Albi%29_Le_Jockey_-_1899_-_Henri_de_Toulouse-Lautrec_-_Mus%C3%A9e_Toulouse-Lautrec.jpg/1280px-%28Albi%29_Le_Jockey_-_1899_-_Henri_de_Toulouse-Lautrec_-_Mus%C3%A9e_Toulouse-Lautrec.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/%28Albi%29_Le_Jockey_-_1899_-_Henri_de_Toulouse-Lautrec_-_Mus%C3%A9e_Toulouse-Lautrec.jpg/500px-%28Albi%29_Le_Jockey_-_1899_-_Henri_de_Toulouse-Lautrec_-_Mus%C3%A9e_Toulouse-Lautrec.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Toulouse-Lautrec – The Jockey (1899)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A(Albi)_Le_Jockey_-_1899_-_Henri_de_Toulouse-Lautrec_-_Mus%C3%A9e_Toulouse-Lautrec.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Racecourse_In_Chester3.jpg/500px-Racecourse_In_Chester3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Racecourse_In_Chester3.jpg/1280px-Racecourse_In_Chester3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_c